# Text files are stored and checked out with LF line endings on every
# platform, so a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf) matches the Mac one and the
# tests that read files as text see the same bytes. PowerShell scripts stay
# ASCII as well (Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a file without a BOM as the
# ANSI code page). From IHS DataLab's .gitattributes at 6b6fdca.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Windows' own script formats keep CRLF (none are committed today; the
# installer writes bin\um-codex.cmd with CRLF itself).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.whl binary
*.zip binary
